ea526-688a-4bb8-ad2e-6ba6e6da52ac/tasks/b2zf4gmbb.output\"; do sleep 10; done; echo done"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":3,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":3,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"material":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":68,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle 96 is closed: the parallel For loop copy (`par1359`) made frame loss worse, and the real per-frame cost turned out to be one panel graph, so cycle 97 builds a version that redraws it less often.\n\n- **ABBA timing run (96-1, 53/0 gates, 15 beads, 120 s):**\n  - The unmodified copy (S1) lost 3,435 and 3,389 frames.\n  - `par1359` lost 3,867 and 3,863, about 13 % more.\n  - `par1359` is rejected and will not be shipped, so the rule-1a replay was not needed.\n- **Review of the failed prediction (96-2):** the reviewer refuted it, and I accepted that. The likely causes, none measured: a non-reentrant subVI (`Magnet2Force`) forcing the iterations to run one at a time, the parallel loop taking every CPU core, and memory work that does not speed up with more cores.\n- **Where #1359's output goes (96-3, offline):** only to the front-panel graph \"Force (pN) vs Extension (nm)\". Nothing reaches the saved tra file, the motors or the tracking kernel. At 15 beads that graph costs about 10 ms of every frame, against an 11.1 ms camera period.\n- **Next lever (plan item PD205):** keep adding to the history every frame, but redraw the graph only every N frames.\n  - N is a new panel control, default 9 (about 10 Hz).\n  - N = 1 behaves exactly like today, and that setting anchors the rule-1a check.\n  - It is accepted only after a replay at N = 1 matches S1 exactly.\n- **Question for the user (D-2026-09-26-02):** is it OK for that graph to redraw about 10 times a second? The default of 9 is an assumption until you answer. If you say no, the default becomes 1 and this speed-up is lost.\n- **Close:** `next.json` is valid, and it follows the outcome-review steer: the next act is a build and a run. STATUS `## NEXT` is rewritten. The retrospective ran last and its findings are recorded in the review file. It named one fault: the review-card reader rejects the \"unknown cost\" (`?`) form that our own reviewers are told to use. The fix is a small card in cycle 97, after the build.\n\nLabVIEW was confirmed closed at the end of the timing run.","ttft_ms":1934,"type":"result","duration_ms":4782527,"uuid":"f3967f4c-a2fe-46f6-bd2c-b1471228d6af","ttft_stream_ms":1789,"time_to_request_ms":235,"first_content_frame_ms":1789,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
